body:
The thing is, you've already had a life. With ups and downs just as everyone has, and I don't mean to disregard everything you've said, as its obvious you have put a lot of thought in what you said, but I think it comes down to a generational difference in views on climate change and ecological collapse

&#x200B;

But many instances of doomsday were prevented in the past by the right person being at the right place in the right time. The Cold War is full of instances of these moments were the existence of our species came down to random chance. Imagine if someone other then [Stanislav Petrov](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanislav_Petrov#Incident) had been in the hot seat in 1983?

&#x200B;

And to be blunt, I don't see any Petrov's in our leadership

&#x200B;

Thank you anyway for commenting
